# TileSmith build settings (read automatically by npm in this folder).
# Each omit[] line tells npm not to install one kind of extra package. Nothing here changes the finished app.
#
# omit[]=optional
#   Skips optional proxy helpers used only to download Electron through a corporate proxy
#   (global-agent via electron-builder's @electron/get 3.x, and undici). global-agent pulls in
#   roarr -> sprintf-js, which has an advisory with no fix released yet (GHSA-hp3w-g68c-fv3c).
#   npm audit fix --force would instead downgrade electron-builder to a version with high/critical issues.
#
# omit[]=peer
#   Skips electron-builder's add-on for "Squirrel.Windows" installers (electron-builder-squirrel-windows).
#   TileSmith builds a portable exe (or NSIS installer / Mac dmg), and electron-builder only loads that
#   add-on for the "squirrel" target. Its chain electron-winstaller -> temp -> rimraf 2 -> glob 7 -> inflight
#   is what printed the "npm warn deprecated" lines. dmg-builder (Mac) is still installed because
#   electron-builder depends on it directly.
#
# To undo either one: delete its line, then run  npm run clean  and  npm install.
omit[]=optional
omit[]=peer
